{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Density-Reachable Cluster.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Density-Reachable Cluster.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"density reachable cluster density reachable cluster","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Density-Reachable Cluster.md","fileName":"Density-Reachable Cluster.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Density-Reachable Cluster","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 21:34\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Density and Grid-Based Clustering]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Density and Grid-Based Clustering","dataclustering.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Density-Reachable Cluster.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Density-Reachable Cluster.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"density reachable cluster density reachable cluster","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Density-Reachable Cluster.md","fileName":"Density-Reachable Cluster.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Density-Reachable Cluster","heading":"Density-Reachable Cluster","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Density reachability defines a cluster through chains of sufficiently populated neighborhoods. A core observation has enough neighbors within a fixed radius, and another observation is density-reachable when a sequence of core-mediated steps connects them.\n\nThis relation allows dense regions of arbitrary shape to become clusters while isolated observations remain noise. A single radius and minimum-neighbor threshold can struggle when different parts of the dataset have substantially different densities.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Density and Grid-Based Clustering","dataclustering.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Density-Reachable Cluster.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Density-Reachable Clus